sql("SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s'")
sql("CREATE TABLE trusted_device_revocations (user_id uuid PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, revoked_at timestamptz NOT NULL)")
# PostgreSQL is required by this fork (including the existing tenant partial indexes).
# No drain: CREATE TABLE ... REFERENCES users takes a brief lock on users, bounded by the 5 s
# lock_timeout, and the init container retries. The race a drain would guard (an old pod
# recreating trust after a revocation) needs a revocation during the Hanko rollout; the only
# caller of the revocation route is clinic-os#8469, which deploys after this image.
